{"name":"Fair Winds","hex":"#f3e6d6","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fair winds","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of fair wind"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fair_winds"}],"entries":[{"title":"Fair","blocks":[{"text":"A fair is gathering of people for a variety of entertainment or commercial activities. Fairs are typically temporary with scheduled times lasting from an afternoon to several weeks. Fairs showcase a wide range of goods, products, and services, and often include competitions, exhibitions, and educational activities. Fairs can be thematic, focusing on specific industries or interests."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/2008Overview1.JPG/330px-2008Overview1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fair"},{"title":"Wind","blocks":[{"text":"Wind is the natural movement of air or other gases relative to a planet's surface. Winds occur on a range of scales, from thunderstorm flows lasting tens of minutes, to local breezes generated by heating of land surfaces and lasting a few hours, to global winds resulting from the difference in absorption of solar energy between the climate zones on Earth. The study of wind is known as anemology."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Cherry_tree_moving_in_the_wind_1.gif/330px-Cherry_tree_moving_in_the_wind_1.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wind"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Fairgames.jpg/500px-Fairgames.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Fairgames.jpg/1280px-Fairgames.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Fairgames.jpg/500px-Fairgames.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A boy at the fish pond, the Rockton World's Fair, harvest festival, Canada, 2010","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFairgames.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Goose_Fair_Roundabout.jpg/500px-Goose_Fair_Roundabout.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Goose_Fair_Roundabout.jpg/500px-Goose_Fair_Roundabout.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Roundabouts (also known as a carousel or merry-go-round) are traditional attractions, often seen at fairs.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGoose_Fair_Roundabout.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/1590_Mostaert_Dorfkirmes_anagoria.JPG/500px-1590_Mostaert_Dorfkirmes_anagoria.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/1590_Mostaert_Dorfkirmes_anagoria.JPG/1280px-1590_Mostaert_Dorfkirmes_anagoria.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/1590_Mostaert_Dorfkirmes_anagoria.JPG/500px-1590_Mostaert_Dorfkirmes_anagoria.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Village fair by Flemish artist Gillis Mostaert 1590","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A1590_Mostaert_Dorfkirmes_anagoria.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Delaware_State_Fair_2009.jpg/500px-Delaware_State_Fair_2009.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Delaware_State_Fair_2009.jpg/500px-Delaware_State_Fair_2009.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.o